#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064093 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064225 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7bd68b3-56ae-57e5-81ef-2370c96664c4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] :question/id #uuid "15473603-5bb5-5a20-8fc9-e4d7589ccb38" :question/math-academy-id "e-473" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sin x}\\left(\\cot x + \\sin^2 x\\right)\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\dfrac{1}{\\sin x } = \\csc x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064094 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] :question/id #uuid "68d2eb66-87ab-5182-9669-376bd1f70673" :question/math-academy-id "e-474" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x =  \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\dfrac{\\sin x }{\\cos x}  = \\tan x$ and $\\dfrac{1}{\\cos x} = \\sec x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\textrm d x,\n$$\n\nwhich is a standard trigonometric integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064095 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using Identities and Substitution"}] :question/id #uuid "b34db891-0676-505c-9ba3-57d86f1d9b94" :question/math-academy-id "e-475" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\tan 2x = \\dfrac{\\sin 2x}{\\cos 2x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\int \\dfrac{\\sin{2x}}{\\cos 2x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nNotice that the numerator of the integrand is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we can solve this by substitution.\n\nLet $u=\\cos 2x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-2 \\sin 2x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u= \\sin 2x \\, \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)^{-1}|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using Identities and Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2015152c-6dd4-56e6-906d-eca5aee8113b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431060} {:answer/id #uuid "64b06414-fa24-5496-803e-0ac49b1edb16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431070} {:answer/id #uuid "8054347c-d721-5221-af8e-16ee957f8128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431073} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf286e8-c095-5023-811d-f2ea8779fe1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431078} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e9383f-e46d-5cc2-b821-2e62b2d63f2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bf286e8-c095-5023-811d-f2ea8779fe1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431078} :answer-field/id #uuid "92469112-1ed0-55aa-bae5-7ad7d5ef9904" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a60367e9-cec6-56ff-bdf1-1a7368d63d95" :question/math-academy-id "q-10040" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)}\\frac{1}{u}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1| \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431120 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using Identities and Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fc34fbe-0ac6-5122-9d50-7ed8124d6804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431058} {:answer/id #uuid "229fc38f-7a75-5c2c-bdb9-4a89c232f57e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431061} {:answer/id #uuid "4e22d3f7-480b-5511-8fa6-2677b36f174d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431067} {:answer/id #uuid "c810647a-c42a-522a-8d4e-5301429d057c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431086} {:answer/id #uuid "fa7daa64-9324-5510-bf53-292b940a1d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fc34fbe-0ac6-5122-9d50-7ed8124d6804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431058} :answer-field/id #uuid "e27fa184-c2a1-506b-ac6d-5109a0a21c79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f01d9ac9-bb7d-5b0c-be19-2dc05bc65cd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114295" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,⟹\\,-2\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431110 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064225 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7bd68b3-56ae-57e5-81ef-2370c96664c4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "250b85cf-f9d6-591c-929e-2bd040932967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431062} {:answer/id #uuid "509e529a-c315-525e-8dd6-81ff51ba0502" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431068} {:answer/id #uuid "63d630c2-d867-5897-a83c-5179a2334d2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431069} {:answer/id #uuid "d2651229-f5ff-524e-ae48-22a82959fa2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431089} {:answer/id #uuid "f748e060-6e5e-5da9-b6ea-84a0653e22cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "509e529a-c315-525e-8dd6-81ff51ba0502" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431068} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec74a8fe-dc16-5d8a-9024-ad8266707d7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c4f53f7-a91f-5a87-b60c-2cd20463d6e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-114301" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot 2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot 2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ce83bb5-48a8-5755-a136-3a2157d2ef78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431057} {:answer/id #uuid "854da0b1-b538-5abb-9128-538e7a7c49e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431075} {:answer/id #uuid "bb236701-7224-5bb8-9211-7b2730f8e9b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431083} {:answer/id #uuid "c6086863-df11-58f0-9fa7-5134443d4b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431085} {:answer/id #uuid "ee6b0533-0ce9-53e9-9ea2-abb22d26246a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6086863-df11-58f0-9fa7-5134443d4b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431085} :answer-field/id #uuid "aca77544-0046-5524-9cef-1c8e548a94a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a4cd24e-1cbf-547b-aab3-c78dc742ec94" :question/math-academy-id "q-114308" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{3}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{3}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}({tan}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that ${tan}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}-{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{3}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}-{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}-\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2621a51d-6ea2-5c0c-b0e8-ef9a5309fa09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247760} {:answer/id #uuid "679c8c73-db45-58a5-8311-c18d1aa796b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248353} {:answer/id #uuid "a8bb94e3-7ab2-5067-a9f7-907364396e08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248924} {:answer/id #uuid "cc6ee47a-69b2-58b2-804c-4404e96412f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249242} {:answer/id #uuid "e05fabc1-bec3-5016-a5ff-3dafd2caba5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "679c8c73-db45-58a5-8311-c18d1aa796b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248353} :answer-field/id #uuid "580bbc55-c5cf-5ded-aa0f-fb666956d730" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e6eaf6d0-3cca-5bcd-87e4-c38716de9570" :question/math-academy-id "q-114313" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431114 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02b90dc2-4752-56a7-9b8f-d500c9d40dff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431054} {:answer/id #uuid "1fc5523c-58ee-55e0-80dd-791ed4446cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431059} {:answer/id #uuid "a842be8e-7dd8-5330-8aa6-c7e1963f7629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431079} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c701b6-77f3-5b86-8e8d-cbfebc97a0af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431084} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc2a33e-12cb-5317-9535-02af0caa9a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffc2a33e-12cb-5317-9535-02af0caa9a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431098} :answer-field/id #uuid "07a0cda5-2de4-5cc2-802a-a5549d6da26a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8cd683e0-e43d-570b-a907-b426c76c1c6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-114319" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0] \\\\  & =-[\\frac{1}{2}-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431113 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1161462-0f9d-545a-a5a5-27e6a35427ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1161462-0f9d-545a-a5a5-27e6a35427ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431092} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fe9e96d-c290-5de0-aea5-06fc2a18c7e7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77e54e57-de69-5688-a9c9-dfe71c2ce5e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-352711" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identities $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using Identities and Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c4c17b5-6041-5b4a-921e-16d5b13a2a5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319573} {:answer/id #uuid "da2d4300-1fc2-5499-8622-53086d327657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da2d4300-1fc2-5499-8622-53086d327657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431090} :answer-field/id #uuid "786408a1-4911-5c78-8041-0f51f924f24b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "00fe6411-9f3d-58f9-a531-7305d81e2e57" :question/math-academy-id "q-352797" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3/2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1}^{3/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064225 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7bd68b3-56ae-57e5-81ef-2370c96664c4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4783ae01-0409-5f42-a49a-a5011eafe80c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4783ae01-0409-5f42-a49a-a5011eafe80c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431065} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8cb6fe3-1966-59eb-9541-67fe64eb26b5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cdc94a5e-ffa3-5e3c-b067-8b7e71e5c799" :question/math-academy-id "q-358219" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}3\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x{cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}3\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x{cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=2x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-sin\\,(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064225 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7bd68b3-56ae-57e5-81ef-2370c96664c4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86a74f3d-6597-59e4-b81c-8406532b8b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86a74f3d-6597-59e4-b81c-8406532b8b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431076} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a251513-9691-50f6-b973-f2685262f1ed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431100}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d54d59da-aeb4-5592-b790-f9a9feee5b10" :question/math-academy-id "q-358220" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}\\frac{9}{{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}\\frac{9}{{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}9{(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}9{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=3x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=3x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{9}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}9{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =9{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡u{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =3(\\sqrt{3}-1) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}-3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using Identities and Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4afbb947-1a46-57c3-a2dc-395ab6315772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4afbb947-1a46-57c3-a2dc-395ab6315772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431066} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c69fd7b-4aa9-5d3d-a2cf-a03772cdb2a1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dadcc805-1744-58ea-b449-313016666d23" :question/math-academy-id "q-362158" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /24}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{24}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /24}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /24}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064225 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7bd68b3-56ae-57e5-81ef-2370c96664c4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8eef9722-f326-5995-94aa-696c6de0feb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431077} {:answer/id #uuid "ab45b025-5861-5024-8958-4ef3403a84cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431080} {:answer/id #uuid "c9711a7d-8c7c-54ef-b29c-11352c7fb2db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431087} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6108cc-2a4c-50ea-9d2d-80ef3ef54486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431088} {:answer/id #uuid "f002d208-93d4-565e-847d-55497116f0c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f002d208-93d4-565e-847d-55497116f0c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431094} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd13680e-c437-5191-a0b8-f472cae34b1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4246a553-248d-558d-9e27-dac3cd88b439" :question/math-academy-id "q-49271" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cot}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity ${cot}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cot}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({csc}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064225 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7bd68b3-56ae-57e5-81ef-2370c96664c4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fc5237a-c69b-55ae-b866-010d3f7a5bd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330371} {:answer/id #uuid "3cd1cdcd-2921-5ddc-b909-e7e993685c9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330489} {:answer/id #uuid "50fef89f-04e0-57c1-8ae4-fc0b3a91c400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330683} {:answer/id #uuid "8245d36a-a259-5c47-8ea5-6c5ffebba5d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331100} {:answer/id #uuid "912e4360-a6f3-5690-971b-e8aa27cc95d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8245d36a-a259-5c47-8ea5-6c5ffebba5d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331100} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e525583-0340-50af-b1e3-515ea118e8bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c28e3047-44ec-5cae-a521-e1a19c0409df" :question/math-academy-id "q-49274" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431116 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using Identities and Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05f4f35f-6fb8-5362-bb51-1c0b0c319dc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431055} {:answer/id #uuid "14b36ff5-eeb9-52d4-b7b8-21c79368f8b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26\\sqrt{3}}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431056} {:answer/id #uuid "41aaf43b-2c95-50cf-a8a3-79ae4c22104b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431064} {:answer/id #uuid "85271a33-9aae-5b9d-a3b8-a96dd470bdac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14\\sqrt{3}}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431074} {:answer/id #uuid "dcaf3e71-8a60-5d8e-be80-97ff5b0a7a92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14b36ff5-eeb9-52d4-b7b8-21c79368f8b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26\\sqrt{3}}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431056} :answer-field/id #uuid "82084fd2-bb79-5568-8b5b-a9fbb9530769" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c26cdc41-d401-5858-96e0-ffa4a20294ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-49279" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,du={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{\\sqrt{3}}{u}^{2}\\,\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}{|}_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({(\\sqrt{3})}^{3}-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(3\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}(3-\\frac{1}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{26\\sqrt{3}}{27}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Trigonometric Functions Using Trigonometric Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ade44e9-b6f9-500e-bc09-791aec3c4112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431063} {:answer/id #uuid "6590c99b-1fe0-54a5-9f86-8aebcedc658b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431071} {:answer/id #uuid "6d4d7986-64b5-5587-b804-bab2a0930585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431072} {:answer/id #uuid "ae2dad62-d368-5197-b93b-e3e45fe17653" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431081} {:answer/id #uuid "fd953cc5-abf5-5b0c-84f3-3e4672a326d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6590c99b-1fe0-54a5-9f86-8aebcedc658b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431071} :answer-field/id #uuid "e803221b-b806-5450-a5a1-2379c91d357f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49b73c78-3335-57b5-a631-c7f8dd771090" :question/math-academy-id "q-73365" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(1-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
